---
import { fmt } from '../screens/ios';

const DAYS = 28;
// A week logged to the calorie, then nothing.
const precise = [2187, 1964, 2203, 2241, 2176, 2090, 2318];
// Every day logged, roughly. A few run over, like the orange bars in the app's adherence chart.
const over = new Set([9, 19, 24]);

const cell = 'h-9 rounded-[9px] sm:h-11 sm:rounded-[11px]';
---

<section id="why" class="px-3 sm:px-4" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="reveal rounded-card bg-surface px-6 py-20 text-center sm:px-12 sm:py-32">
    <p class="eyebrow text-ios-orange">Why it works</p>
    <h2 id="why-title" class="display mx-auto mt-6 max-w-5xl text-[clamp(2.6rem,6.6vw,5.75rem)]">
      Roughly right every day beats perfectly right for a week.
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-xl">
      You don't need to know that dinner was 612 calories. Knowing it was about 600, and that you're landing near
      your goal most days, is what actually moves the needle.
    </p>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-xl">
      Weighing and logging every gram turns food into homework, and it's easy for the numbers to take over. Macro is
      built for being mindful, not meticulous: quick enough to keep up, and easier on your head.
    </p>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-16 grid max-w-5xl gap-3 text-left sm:mt-20 sm:gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <figure class="rounded-[2rem] bg-white p-6 sm:p-9">
        <figcaption class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
          <span class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]">Perfectly right</span>
          <span class="text-[15px] text-faint">7 of {DAYS} days</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div
          role="img"
          aria-label="Seven days logged to the calorie, then three weeks with nothing logged"
          class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-7 gap-1.5 sm:gap-2"
        >
          {
            Array.from({ length: DAYS }, (_, i) =>
              i < precise.length ? (
                <span class={`${cell} grid place-items-center bg-ink text-[10px] font-medium text-white tabular-nums sm:text-xs`}>
                  {fmt(precise[i])}
                </span>
              ) : (
                <span class={`${cell} border border-dashed border-ink/15`} />
              ),
            )
          }
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Every gram weighed, every barcode scanned. Then it all got a bit much.
        </p>
      </figure>

      <figure class="rounded-[2rem] bg-white p-6 sm:p-9">
        <figcaption class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
          <span class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]">Roughly right</span>
          <span class="text-[15px] text-faint">{DAYS} of {DAYS} days</span>
        </figcaption>
        <div
          role="img"
          aria-label={`All ${DAYS} days logged, most of them close to the goal and a few over it`}
          class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-7 gap-1.5 sm:gap-2"
        >
          {Array.from({ length: DAYS }, (_, i) => <span class={`${cell} ${over.has(i) ? 'bg-[#f2a144]/90' : 'bg-ios-green/80'}`} />)}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          About 600 here, about 400 there. A few days over, and still on track.
        </p>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
